--- !u!114 &2053972843
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2053972842}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cf49c1c9e31937a449601db136d94106, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ColliderEditor.Demo.ColliderEditorDemoNotes
  notes: "COLLIDER EDITOR DEMO\n====================\nThe six objects under 'Demo
    Objects' have meshes but NO colliders.\nPress Play once to see the yellow test
    balls fall straight through them, then stop Play mode and follow the steps below.\n\nTRY
    IT\n1. Open the tool:  Tools > Apollo Utilities > Collider Editor\n2. Select
    an object in the Hierarchy (for example '1 - Stairs').\n3. Click 'Create Object
    Collider' in the Collider Editor window.\n4. In the Scene view, pick vertices:\n    
    - Click a vertex to toggle it\n     - Drag a rectangle to select many\n     -
    Shift+drag adds, Ctrl/Cmd+drag removes\n     - Double-click selects the whole
    connected piece\n     - Ctrl/Cmd+A selects everything, H hides the selection,
    Shift+H isolates it\n5. Choose a collider type (Sphere, Capsule, Box, Cylinder,
    Mesh From Selected Vertices, Convex Decomposition).\n   A live preview is drawn
    in the Scene view (not for Convex Decomposition).\n6. Click 'Create Collider'
    (or press Ctrl/Cmd+Enter) and confirm the dialog. Ctrl/Cmd+1..6 picks a type
    and creates it with no dialog.\n7. Repeat with different selections to build
    a compound collider. Esc or 'Stop Editing Collider' finishes.\n8. Press Play
    again: the balls should now land on your colliders.\n\nWHAT TO TRY ON EACH OBJECT\n 
    1 - Stairs   Box colliders on groups of steps, or a single Mesh From Selected
    Vertices\n  2 - Ring     Convex Decomposition (a single convex collider would
    fill the hole)\n  3 - Table    Box on the top and on each leg, or Convex Decomposition\n 
    4 - Pillar   Capsule (try the different Capsule Fit methods)\n  5 - Barrel  
    Cylinder (try different side counts)\n  6 - Boulder  Sphere (compare Sphere Fit
    methods)\n\nTIPS\n- Open 'Generated Colliders' in the window and turn on Performance
    View to see every collider colour-coded by cost (blue = fastest, red = slowest).\n-
    Ctrl/Cmd+Z undoes selection and creation.\n- Mesh-based colliders are saved as
    mesh assets next to this scene. Delete them from the Generated Colliders list,
    not from the Project window.\n"
